(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// Traceback and frame objects' attributes (Python/traceback.c, Objects/frameobject.c)."] [31 53 "// in bytes (2 × the instruction), the reported one after a reraise N"] [61 2 "// the attributes as the type's getset descriptors too (type(frame).f_locals: inspect.isgetsetdescriptor; dir)"] [81 1 "// FrameLocals is f_locals (frame_locals_get_impl): a module's or class's namespace (its mapping when __prepare__'s or"] [82 1 "// exec's was not a dict), else PEP 667's write-through proxy over the frame's fast locals, cells and free variables."] [90 1 "// frameNamespace is a module's or class's body's namespace (its mapping when not a dict), nil for a function's frame,"] [91 1 "// and nil while an inlined comprehension of the body has its own names bound (PEP 709's hidden locals: CPython's"] [92 1 "// _PyFrame_HasHiddenLocals, the proxy then over them and the extra locals)."] [108 1 "// frameSetAttr is frame's setters (f_trace, f_trace_lines, f_trace_opcodes, f_lineno) and its read-only attributes'"] [109 1 "// refusals, as frameobject.c's getset and member tables answer them; v nil: del."] [144 3 "// frame_lineno_set_impl: a jump from a trace function's event (trace.go; queue 219t)"] [152 1 "// frameExecuting is f running: on the current thread's chain of frames, or a running generator's."] [167 1 "// frameClear is frame.clear() (frame_clear_impl): an executing or suspended frame refused; a generator's not started"] [168 1 "// closed; else the locals, cells, value stack, extra locals and f_trace dropped (frame_tp_clear), the code, globals,"] [169 1 "// builtins and f_back kept."] [195 1 "// FrameLocalsProxy is frame.f_locals of a function's frame (PEP 667; Objects/frameobject.c's PyFrameLocalsProxy_Type):"] [196 1 "// a mapping over the frame itself, reads and writes going to its fast locals and cells, so a write is seen by the"] [197 1 "// frame's code at its next load (the loop's and the compiled code's loads read f.Fast and f.Cells, never a copy:"] [198 1 "// survey \"Design: 219\"); a name none of the code's goes to the frame's extra locals."] [201 1 "// FrameLocalsProxyType is the proxy's type (\"FrameLocalsProxy\", registered as a Mapping by _collections_abc)."] [206 1 "// frameSlot is one of a code's names in co_localsplusnames' order: the fast locals (a parameter that is a cell read"] [207 1 "// through its cell), then the cells that are no parameter, then the free variables."] [210 18 "// the index in f.Fast or f.Cells, -1 for the other"] [211 18 "// an earlier slot has the name (each)"] [247 1 "// slotValue is s's value in f, nil when unbound."] [276 1 "// slotOf is framelocalsproxy_getkeyindex: the slot of key's name, an exact str by its text, else any key by its hash"] [277 1 "// and ==; read: only a bound one. -1 when none."] [329 1 "// set is framelocalsproxy_setitem (v nil: del): a local's slot written, never removed; else the extra locals."] [361 1 "// each calls fn on the bound names and their values in order, then the extra locals'. A name twice among the slots"] [362 1 "// (an inlined comprehension's own name in a fast slot beside the function's cell of that name, while the comprehension"] [363 1 "// runs: GH-128396's case, one slot in CPython holding the plain value) gives its first bound slot's value."] [389 1 "// dict is the proxy's items as a new dict (PyDict_Update(dict, proxy))."] [401 1 "// merge is framelocalsproxy_merge: other a dict or a proxy, each of its keys set; false for another mapping."] [501 2 "// nb_or: either operand the proxy, the result a dict of the left's items, then the right's"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[69 42] [84 28] [157 25] [158 19] [158 29] [177 15] [178 25] [285 24] [295 22] [317 21] [318 26] [368 25] [370 14] [370 38] [378 19] [379 44] [404 39] [406 34] [411 26] [422 24] [435 35] [468 36] [475 31] [508 37] [515 25] [527 31] [534 41] [540 43] [548 42] [556 41] [562 49] [566 27] [566 34] [572 43] [617 40] [629 22] [6